{#
  THE ONE PAGE ARCHITECTURE — Design's 2026-10-05 property package.

  Six pages, shared by every theme. A theme file sets the eight typography
  variables below and includes this; nothing else differs between themes
  (Design: "they differ only in display/body typeface, weight, tracking, case
  and corner radius").

  WHY THIS IS A SHARED FILE AND NOT COPIED PER THEME
  `test_one_comp_set.py::test_the_live_template_set_is_the_five_entry_files`
  used to fail on any live template with an `extends`, `import`, `include` or
  `from`. That gate exists because of D-131: there is a second property
  template tree under `_base/` that renders NOWHERE, and three separate costs
  were paid reading it as if it did. The gate is changed deliberately, which
  Design's README asks for by name, and it is NARROWED rather than dropped —
  a live template may reach `_v2/` and may still not reach `_base/`. The
  distinction the gate protects is "is this file rendered", not "does this
  file use include".

  CLASSES, NOT THE DESIGN FILE'S INLINE STYLES. The contrast ratchet keys on
  `(family, selector, fg, bg)`; with everything inline every selector is
  `div` and 118 baseline entries become unreadable. The values below are the
  design's, to the pixel.

  VARIABLES THE THEME FILE MUST SET, all consumed as CSS custom properties:
    t_display, t_body        font stacks
    t_display_weight         300-900
    t_display_tracking       em
    t_display_case           none | uppercase
    t_radius                 px
    t_font_link              the Google Fonts href
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ language | default('en', true) }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ doc.report_kind }} — {{ doc.street }}</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ t_font_link }}">
<style>
  :root {
    /* The derive_theme tokens. Nothing on this document is a colour that is
       not one of these or a fixed neutral below (Design §3.1). `display_ink`
       is declared below, next to the decision it records. */
    --primary: {{ primary }};
    --primary-dark: {{ primary_dark }};
    --primary-ink: {{ primary_ink }};
    --on-primary: {{ on_primary }};
    --tint: {{ tint }};
    --primary-on-dark: {{ primary_on_dark }};
    /* Rule lines on a primary fill, by which way on_primary resolved. */
    --on-primary-rule: {% if on_primary | lower == '#ffffff' %}rgba(255,255,255,0.3){% else %}rgba(20,21,26,0.25){% endif %};

    /* ── CLOSED, 2026-10-07, BY DESIGN DERIVING IT. ──────────────────────
       This was an open [JERRY] decision. Design's package specified `#FFFFFF`
       for the cover's display lines — street, city, the four 30px stat values
       — "by owner decision", on the stated grounds that white "passes the 3.0
       large-text threshold" on the sample brands. D-171 measured that and the
       premise was false for two of six: amber #f59e0b is 2.15 and lime
       #84cc16 is 1.98, clearing neither 3.0 nor 4.5.

       The holding position was `on_primary`, which passes on all six but
       overshoots: it picks the strict winner between white and near-black, so
       it also took white OFF teal, where white is 3.74 and the owner exception
       was real. The note recorded that taking Design's decision as written
       would widen the exception from one brand to four. Neither was right.

       Design's answer (RESPONSE_2026-10-06) is a THIRD option, and it is the
       correct one: compute the threshold instead of asserting it.

           display_ink = contrast(white, primary) >= 3.0 ? white : on_primary

       Which lands, measured on `themes.derive_theme`:

           brand   white  near-black   on_primary   display_ink
           violet   5.70        3.20      #ffffff       #ffffff
           cyan     5.36        3.40      #ffffff       #ffffff
           red      4.83        3.77      #ffffff       #ffffff
           teal     3.74        4.87      #14151a       #ffffff   <- differs
           amber    2.15        8.49      #14151a       #14151a
           lime     1.98        9.23      #14151a       #14151a

       So it keeps white on exactly the one brand the owner exception was
       about, and drops it on exactly the two that failed. One brand wide, not
       four and not zero — and derived, so a seventh brand resolves itself. */
    --display-ink: {{ display_ink }};
    --cover-display: var(--display-ink);

    /* Fixed neutrals, with the measured contrast on white. */
    --ink: #14161A;        /* 18.1:1 */
    --body: #2A2D33;       /* 13.8:1 */
    --muted: #5E636B;      /* 6.05:1 — the lightest text on the surface */
    --rule: #ECECE8;
    --rule-soft: #E4E4E0;
    --rule-axis: #D9DADF;
    --track: #F1F1EE;
    --strip: #F6F6F3;
    --inactive: #EDEDEA;
    --dark: {{ doc.dark }};

    --display: {{ t_display }};
    --body-face: {{ t_body }};
    --display-weight: {{ t_display_weight }};
    --display-tracking: {{ t_display_tracking }};
    --display-case: {{ t_display_case }};
    --radius: {{ t_radius }};
  }

  @page { size: Letter; margin: 0; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    font-family: var(--body-face);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  /* 8.5 x 11in at 96dpi. Fixed height, not min-height: every page in this
     document is a fixed-row layout and a page that grows is a page that
     pushes a footer onto the next sheet. */
  .sheet {
    width: 816px;
    height: 1056px;
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
    page-break-after: always;
    page-break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .sheet:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }

  /* PDFShift renders through a headless browser's print path, so the print
     rules are the ones that ship. `@page { margin: 0 }` above removes the
     browser's own margins; this removes the drop shadow and the page gap that
     only make sense on screen, and re-states the breaks so a renderer that
     honours `@media print` over the base rules still gets them.
     `test_has_print_media_query` asserts this block exists on every theme —
     it was missing from the first version of this file, and the gate is the
     only thing that said so. */
  @media print {
    html, body { background: #fff; }
    .sheet {
      box-shadow: none;
      margin: 0;
      page-break-after: always;
      page-break-inside: avoid;
    }
    .sheet:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  }

  /* ── running head and footer, in-page ──────────────────────────────────
     The design specifies these as PDFShift header/footer elements. They are
     rendered in-page here because the property pipeline does not pass
     header_html/footer_html (only the market one does), and because these
     pages are fixed-height — the 1.07in the market reports recovered by
     moving to the header slot comes from reflow, which cannot happen here.
     Moving them is a pipeline change, not a template change. */
  .runhead {
    height: 40px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding: 0 52px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .runhead-address { white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }

  .pagefoot {
    margin: 0 52px;
    padding: 14px 0 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .pagefoot-agent { font-weight: 700; }
  .pagefoot-brand { color: var(--muted); }
  .pagefoot-num { color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

  /* ── shared type ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: var(--display-weight);
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: var(--display-tracking);
    text-transform: var(--display-case);
  }
  .label {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--primary-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .pagehead {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .pagehead-aside { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); text-align: right; }
  .body-pad { padding: 32px 52px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex: 1; min-height: 0; }

  /* ── 1 · cover ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .masthead {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: var(--on-primary);
    padding: 36px 52px 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 26px;
  }
  .masthead-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
  /* No `opacity` on a brand fill: 85% of on_primary over `primary` is a
     colour neither token measured, and the contrast gate reports it as a
     pairing nobody chose. Design's 85%/92%/90% opacities on the band are all
     dropped for the same reason. */
  .masthead-kind { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 600; }
  .masthead-logo { height: 40px; max-width: 200px; object-fit: contain; object-position: right center; }
  .masthead-brand { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .cover-titlebox { height: 78px; display: flex; align-items: flex-end; overflow: hidden; }
  /* White by owner decision, scoped to the display lines. On teal that is
     3.74:1 — above the 3.0 large-text threshold for the street and the 30px
     stat values, and the recorded exception for the 22px city line. */
  .cover-street {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: var(--display-weight);
    font-size: {{ doc.title_size }}px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: var(--display-tracking);
    text-transform: var(--display-case);
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    max-width: 100%;
    color: var(--cover-display);
  }
  /* `opacity` on a brand fill makes the effective colour depend on the fill,
     which is the thing §3.2 forbids — so the city line is a flat token. The
     design's 92% is dropped rather than approximated.

     AND IT IS NOT `--cover-display`. 22px at weight 500 is NOT large text by
     either of WCAG 1.4.3's definitions (>=24px, or >=18.66px at >=700), so it
     needs 4.5 and not 3.0. `display_ink`'s threshold is 3.0, which is right
     for the three sites around it — the street line (32-64px) and the 30px
     stat values — and wrong for this one.

     The pixel gate caught it: pointing all four sites at `display_ink` put
     `#ffffff on #0d9488` at 3.74 under `span.cover-city`, one new failure, on
     teal. Design's rule is correct and is applied to one site too many; the
     city line takes `on_primary`, which is the 4.5-or-better token.

     So the derived threshold is right and the SET OF SITES it covers is the
     part that needed measuring — which is also what Design asked for ("please
     re-measure"). */
  .cover-city { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--on-primary); }
  .cover-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--on-primary-rule);
    padding-top: 16px;
  }
  .cover-stat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; padding-right: 12px; }
  .cover-stat-value {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: var(--display-weight);
    font-size: 30px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: var(--display-tracking);
    color: var(--cover-display);
  }
  .cover-stat-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 500; }

  .cover-body { padding: 24px 52px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px; flex: 1; min-height: 0; }
  .plate { border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; background: var(--tint); position: relative; }
  .plate-hero { flex: 1; min-height: 300px; }
  .plate img { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  /* No text over photography anywhere (§3.2). The missing-photo tile is a
     TINT panel, so its text sits on a known flat colour. */
  .nophoto { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end; padding: 20px; }
  .nophoto-name { font-family: var(--display); font-size: 28px; font-weight: var(--display-weight); line-height: 1; color: var(--primary-ink); }
  .nophoto-note { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 6px; color: var(--muted); }
  .cover-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; padding-bottom: 20px; }
  /* One column when there is no name to address the report to. */
  .cover-grid.is-unaddressed { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .cover-for { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .cover-for-name { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: var(--display-weight); font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: var(--display-tracking); }
  .cover-for-note { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .inshort { background: var(--tint); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 18px 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  /* Four lines, bounded. The only other thing on page 1 that grows with data
     is the title, and the ladder bounds that. */
  .inshort-text { margin: 0; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--body); max-height: 81px; overflow: hidden; }

  /* ── 2 · your home ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .home-photos { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .plate-pair { height: 220px; }
  .plate-caption { position: absolute; left: 12px; bottom: 12px; background: #fff; color: var(--ink); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; padding: 5px 9px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .detail-groups { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0 40px; align-items: start; }
  .detail-group { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .detail-title { font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--primary-ink); font-weight: 600; padding: 14px 0 6px; border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink); }
  .detail-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 12.5px; }
  .detail-label { color: var(--muted); white-space: nowrap; }
  .detail-value { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }
  /* A dash is quieter than a value, deliberately: weight 400 and the muted
     grey, so a page of knowns does not read as a page of maybes. */
  .detail-value.is-absent { font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); }
  .detail-value.is-wrap { white-space: normal; overflow: visible; font-size: 11.5px; }
  .notonrecord { display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: baseline; padding: 14px 16px; background: var(--strip); border-radius: var(--radius); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); }
  .notonrecord-label { font-weight: 700; white-space: nowrap; }

  /* ── 3 · comparable sales ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .conf-wrap { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-end; gap: 6px; }
  .conf-pill { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 600; padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--tint); color: var(--primary-ink); white-space: nowrap; }
  .conf-grade { width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--primary); color: var(--on-primary); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; }
  .comp-grid { flex: 1; min-height: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); grid-template-rows: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px 16px; }
  .comp { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; }
  .comp-plate { position: relative; flex: 1; min-height: 0; border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; background: var(--tint); }
  .comp-plate img { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  /* Solid white plate on the photo — never text directly on photography. */
  .comp-price { position: absolute; left: 10px; top: 10px; background: #fff; color: var(--ink); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .comp-nophoto { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end; padding: 12px; }
  .comp-nophoto-name { font-family: var(--display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: var(--display-weight); line-height: 1; color: var(--primary-ink); }
  .comp-nophoto-note { font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 4px; color: var(--muted); }
  .comp-lines { padding-top: 9px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; }
  .comp-address { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .comp-line { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); }

  /* ── 4 · what the comparable sales support ────────────────────────── */
  .rangepanel { background: var(--dark); color: #fff; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 28px 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; }
  /* primary_on_dark is guaranteed against --dark and against nothing else,
     which is why --dark is the only dark surface on the document. */
  .rangepanel-label { font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--primary-on-dark); font-weight: 600; }
  .rangepanel-figures { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .rangepanel-headline { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: var(--display-weight); font-size: 60px; line-height: 0.95; letter-spacing: var(--display-tracking); white-space: nowrap; }
  .rangepanel-median { font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); }
  .band { position: relative; height: 10px; border-radius: 5px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.14); }
  .band-fill { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; background: var(--primary-on-dark); border-radius: 5px; }
  .band-marker { position: absolute; top: -6px; width: 3px; height: 22px; background: #fff; border-radius: 2px; transform: translateX(-50%); }
  .band-axis { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 11px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); }
  .band-axis-mid { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }
  .rangepanel-note { margin: 0; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); }

  .compare-head, .compare-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 110px 110px 110px 110px; gap: 12px; }
  .compare-head { padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--ink); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .compare-head-subject { text-align: right; color: var(--primary-ink); font-weight: 700; }
  .compare-head-col { text-align: right; }
  .compare-row { padding: 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 13px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .compare-label { color: var(--muted); }
  .compare-subject { text-align: right; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  .compare-cell { text-align: right; }

  .bars { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: {{ doc.bar_gap }}px; }
  .bar-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 170px minmax(0, 1fr) 90px; gap: 12px; align-items: center; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .bar-address { white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .bar-track { height: {{ doc.bar_height }}px; background: var(--track); border-radius: 3px; overflow: hidden; }
  .bar-fill { height: 100%; background: var(--primary); border-radius: 3px; }
  .bar-price { text-align: right; font-weight: 600; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

  /* ── 5 · your market ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .market-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 1.5px solid var(--ink); }
  .market-stat { padding: 22px 16px 22px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; border-right: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .market-stat-value { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: var(--display-weight); font-size: 44px; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: var(--display-tracking); color: var(--ink); }
  .market-stat-value.is-brand { color: var(--primary-ink); }
  .market-stat-label { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .moi { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: 32px; align-items: start; }
  .moi-copy { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
  .moi-headline { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; }
  .moi-note { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); }
  .moi-cells { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(8, 1fr); gap: 4px; height: 44px; }
  .moi-cell { background: var(--inactive); border-radius: 3px; }
  .moi-cell.is-filled { background: var(--primary); }
  .moi-legend { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4fr 2fr 2fr; gap: 4px; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .moi-legend > div { padding-top: 6px; }
  .moi-legend-a { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .moi-legend-b { border-top: 2px solid #B9BBC1; }
  .moi-legend-c { border-top: 2px solid #DADBDF; }
  .chart { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; flex: 1; min-height: 0; }
  .chart-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; }
  .chart-unit { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); }
  .chart-body { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 44px 1fr; gap: 10px; flex: 1; min-height: 0; }
  .chart-yaxis { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; height: 100%; font-size: 10px; color: var(--muted); text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .chart-plot { position: relative; height: 100%; border-left: 1px solid var(--rule-axis); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  .chart-mid { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 50%; border-top: 1px dashed var(--rule-soft); }
  .chart-cols { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 18px; padding: 0 14px; align-items: end; }
  .chart-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 6px; height: 100%; justify-content: flex-end; }
  /* The VALUE above every bar, on every theme. D-126 was a theme that drew
     the chart and printed no numbers on it. */
  .chart-value { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .chart-bar { width: 100%; background: var(--primary-dark); border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; }
  .chart-bar.is-latest { background: var(--primary); }
  .chart-xaxis { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 44px 1fr; gap: 10px; padding-bottom: 24px; }
  .chart-xlabels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 18px; padding: 0 14px; font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--muted); text-align: center; }

  /* ── 6 · next steps ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .agentpanel { background: var(--primary); color: var(--on-primary); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 44px 40px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 28px; align-items: center; }
  .agentpanel-avatar { width: 120px; height: 120px; border-radius: 999px; background: #fff; color: var(--primary-ink); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: var(--display-weight); font-size: 42px; overflow: hidden; }
  .agentpanel-avatar img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .agentpanel-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; min-width: 0; }
  /* `on_primary`, NOT `#FFFFFF`. Design's file sets white here too, but the
     owner decision above is scoped to the cover band — this is page 6's agent
     panel, and nothing recorded an exception for it. Measured at 1.98:1 on
     lime and 2.15:1 on amber before the change. */
  .agentpanel-name { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: var(--display-weight); font-size: 32px; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: var(--display-tracking); color: var(--on-primary); }
  .agentpanel-meta { font-size: 14px; }
  .agentpanel-blurb { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 400px; }
  .agentpanel-contact { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-end; gap: 8px; }
  .agentpanel-phone { background: #fff; color: var(--primary-ink); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: var(--radius); white-space: nowrap; }
  .agentpanel-email { font-size: 13px; }
  .explainers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 40px; padding-top: 8px; }
  .explainer { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .explainer p { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body); }
  .steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; flex: 1; }
  .steps-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
  .step { background: var(--tint); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 18px 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .step-n { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: var(--display-weight); font-size: 30px; line-height: 1; color: var(--primary-ink); }
  .step-title { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; }
  .step-body { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); }
  .disclaimer { padding: 16px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
{% set total_pages = doc.pages | length %}
{% for page in doc.pages %}
{% set page_n = loop.index %}
<section class="sheet sheet-{{ page }}">

  <div class="runhead">
    <span class="runhead-address">Property report · {{ doc.street }}</span>
    <span class="runhead-date">{{ generated_label }}</span>
  </div>

  {% if page == 'cover' %}
  <div class="masthead">
    <div class="masthead-row">
      <span class="masthead-kind">{{ doc.report_kind }}</span>
      {% if agent.logo_url %}
      <img class="masthead-logo" src="{{ agent.logo_url }}" alt="">
      {% else %}
      <span class="masthead-brand">{{ agent.company_name }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="cover-titlebox"><span class="cover-street">{{ doc.street }}</span></div>
      <span class="cover-city">{{ doc.city_line }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cover-stats">
      {% for stat in doc.hero_stats %}
      <div class="cover-stat">
        <span class="cover-stat-value">{{ stat.value }}</span>
        <span class="cover-stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cover-body">
    <div class="plate plate-hero">
      {% if images.hero %}
      <img src="{{ images.hero }}" alt="">
      {% else %}
      <div class="nophoto">
        <span class="nophoto-name">{{ doc.city_name }}</span>
        <span class="nophoto-note">No photo on file</span>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="cover-grid{% if not doc.prepared_for %} is-unaddressed{% endif %}">
      {# NO NAME, NO BLOCK. Jerry: "If the form has no name, the report
         renders without the line. No fallback to the assessor roll." The
         first v2 render printed the LABEL over an empty name, which is the
         same shape as the fallback it forbids — a slot that says a person
         should be here. The grid's other column fills the width. #}
      {% if doc.prepared_for %}
      <div class="cover-for">
        <span class="label">Prepared for</span>
        <span class="cover-for-name">{{ doc.prepared_for }}</span>
        <span class="cover-for-note">{{ doc.prepared_note }}</span>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="inshort">
        <span class="label">In short</span>
        {# The AI narrative, bounded at four lines. When there is none the
           panel says what the report is built from rather than rendering an
           empty paragraph — which is what the first v2 render did, and which
           is valid HTML and so failed nothing. #}
        <p class="inshort-text">{% if overview_text %}{{ overview_text }}{% else %}This report compares {{ doc.comp_count }} recent nearby sales with your home as the public record describes it. The range on page {{ doc.pages.index('range') + 1 if 'range' in doc.pages else 4 }} is what those sales support.{% endif %}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% elif page == 'property' %}
  <div class="body-pad" style="padding-top:28px;gap:18px">
    <div class="pagehead">
      <h2 class="h2">Your home</h2>
      <span class="pagehead-aside">{{ property.full_address }}<br>APN {{ property.apn }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="home-photos">
      <div class="plate plate-pair">
        {% if images.aerial_map %}<img src="{{ images.aerial_map }}" alt="">{% endif %}
        <span class="plate-caption">Aerial</span>
      </div>
      <div class="plate plate-pair">
        {% if cover_image_url %}<img src="{{ cover_image_url }}" alt="">{% endif %}
        <span class="plate-caption">Street view</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="detail-groups">
      {% for group in doc.detail_groups %}
      <div class="detail-group">
        <span class="detail-title">{{ group.title }}</span>
        {% for row in group.rows %}
        {# `is-wrap` on the one row whose value is a legal description:
           everything else on this page is short enough for one nowrap line,
           and "LOT 44 TR#6654 ..." is not. Ellipsising it would hide the
           field rather than show it. #}
        <div class="detail-row">
          <span class="detail-label">{{ row.label }}</span>
          <span class="detail-value{% if row.absent %} is-absent{% endif %}{% if row.wrap %} is-wrap{% endif %}">{{ row.value }}</span>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% if doc.has_unknowns %}
    <div class="notonrecord">
      <span class="notonrecord-label">Not on record</span>
      <span>{{ doc.unknown_list }}. A dash anywhere in this report means the public record doesn't say, not that the answer is no.</span>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {% elif page == 'comparables' %}
  <div class="body-pad" style="gap:20px">
    <div class="pagehead">
      <h2 class="h2">Comparable sales</h2>
      <div class="conf-wrap">
        <span class="conf-pill"><span class="conf-grade">{{ doc.conf_grade }}</span>{{ doc.conf_label }}</span>
        <span class="pagehead-aside">{{ doc.comp_count }} sales within {{ doc.comp_radius }} · {{ doc.comp_window | lower }} · {{ doc.pictured_note }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="comp-grid">
      {% for comp in doc.pictured %}
      <div class="comp">
        <div class="comp-plate">
          {% if comp.photo_url or comp.map_image_url %}
          <img src="{{ comp.photo_url or comp.map_image_url }}" alt="">
          {% else %}
          <div class="comp-nophoto">
            <span class="comp-nophoto-name">{{ comp.neighborhood or doc.city_name }}</span>
            <span class="comp-nophoto-note">No photo on file</span>
          </div>
          {% endif %}
          {# `price_label` is the COLUMN HEADING ("Sale Price" / "List
             Price"). The first render put those two words on every comp
             photo where the price belongs. #}
          <span class="comp-price">{{ comp.price }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="comp-lines">
          <span class="comp-address">{{ comp.address }}</span>
          <span class="comp-line">{{ comp.v2_specs }}</span>
          <span class="comp-line">{{ comp.v2_ppsf }} · {{ comp.v2_dist }} · {{ comp.v2_when }}</span>
          <span class="comp-line">{{ comp.v2_lot }} · {{ comp.v2_hoa }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {% elif page == 'range' %}
  <div class="body-pad" style="padding-top:28px;gap:18px">
    <h2 class="h2">What the comparable sales support</h2>
    <div class="rangepanel">
      <span class="rangepanel-label">Range supported by {{ doc.closed_count }} closed sales · confidence {{ doc.conf_grade }}, {{ doc.conf_label | lower }}</span>
      <div class="rangepanel-figures">
        <span class="rangepanel-headline">{{ doc.range_low }} – {{ doc.range_high }}</span>
        <span class="rangepanel-median">median {{ doc.range_mid }}</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="band">
          {% if doc.band_left is not none %}
          <div class="band-fill" style="left:{{ doc.band_left }}%;right:{{ doc.band_right }}%"></div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if doc.subject_x is not none %}
          <div class="band-marker" style="left:{{ doc.subject_x }}%"></div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="band-axis" style="margin-top:6px">
          <span>{{ doc.axis_low }}</span>
          {% if doc.subject_x is not none %}
          <span class="band-axis-mid">▲ your home's last recorded sale · {{ doc.last_sale_label }}</span>
          {% endif %}
          <span>{{ doc.axis_high }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="rangepanel-note">This is what recent sales of similar homes nearby support. It is a report of the market, not an appraisal, and a listing price is a conversation with your agent.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="compare-head">
        <span></span>
        <span class="compare-head-subject">Your home</span>
        <span class="compare-head-col">Low</span>
        <span class="compare-head-col">Median</span>
        <span class="compare-head-col">High</span>
      </div>
      {% for row in doc.compare_rows %}
      <div class="compare-row">
        <span class="compare-label">{{ row.label }}</span>
        <span class="compare-subject">{{ row.subject }}</span>
        <span class="compare-cell">{{ row.low }}</span>
        <span class="compare-cell">{{ row.mid }}</span>
        <span class="compare-cell">{{ row.high }}</span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="bars">
      <span class="label" style="padding-bottom:4px">Each sale · {{ doc.comp_count }}</span>
      {% for bar in doc.bars %}
      <div class="bar-row">
        <span class="bar-address">{{ bar.address }}</span>
        <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" style="width:{{ bar.width }}%"></div></div>
        <span class="bar-price">{{ bar.price }}</span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {% elif page == 'market_trends' %}
  <div class="body-pad" style="gap:32px">
    <div class="pagehead">
      <h2 class="h2">Your market</h2>
      <span class="pagehead-aside">{{ doc.city_name }} · {{ market_trends.window_label }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="market-stats">
      {% for stat in market_trends.v2_stats %}
      <div class="market-stat">
        <span class="market-stat-value{% if loop.first %} is-brand{% endif %}">{{ stat.value }}</span>
        <span class="market-stat-label">{{ stat.label }}</span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="moi">
      <div class="moi-copy">
        <span class="moi-headline">{{ market_trends.v2_moi_headline }}</span>
        <span class="moi-note">{{ market_trends.v2_moi_note }}</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="moi-cells">
          {% for cell in market_trends.v2_moi_cells %}
          <div class="moi-cell{% if cell %} is-filled{% endif %}"></div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="moi-legend" style="margin-top:8px">
          <div class="moi-legend-a">Seller's · under 4 mo</div>
          <div class="moi-legend-b">Balanced</div>
          <div class="moi-legend-c">Buyer's · 6+</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart">
      <div class="chart-head">
        <span class="label">Median sale price · last 6 months</span>
        <span class="chart-unit">Thousands of dollars</span>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-body">
        <div class="chart-yaxis">
          <span>{{ market_trends.v2_y_top }}</span>
          <span>{{ market_trends.v2_y_mid }}</span>
          <span>{{ market_trends.v2_y_bot }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chart-plot">
          <div class="chart-mid"></div>
          <div class="chart-cols">
            {% for month in market_trends.v2_months %}
            <div class="chart-col">
              <span class="chart-value">{{ month.value }}</span>
              <div class="chart-bar{% if loop.last %} is-latest{% endif %}" style="height:{{ month.height }}%"></div>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-xaxis">
        <span></span>
        <div class="chart-xlabels">
          {% for month in market_trends.v2_months %}<span>{{ month.label }}</span>{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% elif page == 'notes' %}
  <div class="body-pad" style="gap:32px">
    <h2 class="h2">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="agentpanel">
      <div class="agentpanel-avatar">
        {% if agent.photo_url %}<img src="{{ agent.photo_url }}" alt="">{% else %}{{ doc.initials }}{% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="agentpanel-text">
        <span class="agentpanel-name">{{ agent.name }}</span>
        {# `agent.license` is ALREADY formatted ("CA BRE#01234567") by
           `_build_agent_context`; `license_number` is the bare digits.
           Prefixing the formatted one produced "DRE #CA BRE#01234567". #}
        <span class="agentpanel-meta">{{ agent.company_name }}{% if agent.license %} · {{ agent.license }}{% endif %}</span>
        <span class="agentpanel-blurb">{{ doc.agent_blurb }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="agentpanel-contact">
        <span class="agentpanel-phone">{{ agent.phone }}</span>
        <span class="agentpanel-email">{{ agent.email }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="explainers">
      <div class="explainer">
        <span class="label">How the comparables were chosen</span>
        <p>Closed sales within {{ doc.comp_radius }} of your home, {{ doc.comp_window | lower }}, matched on property type and kept within roughly 25% of your home's living area. Listings still on the market are shown for context and not counted in the range.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="explainer">
        <span class="label">Where the data comes from</span>
        <p>Sales and listings from CRMLS, pulled {{ generated_label }}. Property details from the county assessor's public record. A dash means the record is silent, not that the answer is no.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <span class="label">If you're thinking about selling</span>
      <div class="steps-cards">
        {% for step in doc.next_steps %}
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">{{ step.n }}</span>
          <span class="step-title">{{ step.title }}</span>
          <span class="step-body">{{ step.body }}</span>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="disclaimer">Information is deemed reliable but not guaranteed. This report is not an appraisal and is not intended to be relied upon as one. {{ doc.consumer_disclosure }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="pagefoot">
    <span><span class="pagefoot-agent">{{ agent.name }}</span><span class="pagefoot-brand"> · {{ agent.company_name }} · {{ agent.phone }}</span></span>
    <span class="pagefoot-num">Page {{ page_n }} of {{ total_pages }}</span>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}
</body>
</html>
